      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day, usually given as 800 mg three or four times daily. Doses at this level raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth, three times daily**, or another regimen\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you intend, please confirm that. I can enter it with a note recording the clinical rationale, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
